  "text": "Today there is a new worker in the library of Rivertown. His name is Robo Bob, and he is a robot!\n\nRobo Bob is one metre tall. He has big blue eyes and a friendly voice. He helps children to find books. He also says, \"Please be quiet,\" in a very soft voice.\n\nThe children love him. \"He is so funny,\" says eight-year-old Rita. \"He knows every book in the room!\"\n\nThe librarian, Mr Brown, is happy. \"Bob never gets tired,\" he says. \"But he cannot drink tea with me.\" The library is open from nine to six, Monday to Saturday.",
